      "page": "School day & partnership.",
      "heading": "Visitors to Campus",
      "text": "Visitors are expected to sign in through the appropriate school office or secretary and follow campus procedures. Classroom access during lessons is restricted except for authorised school business such as a scheduled parent–teacher conference. Nursery: Monday–Thursday devotion begins at 8:00 a.m.; Friday Chapel is scheduled in the morning. Core lessons run through the morning with a break, and Nursery closes at 1:00 p.m. Kindergarten clubs, enhancement, sport and after-school care appear on designated days. Primary: Monday begins with Assembly. Tuesday includes Mental Drill and Bible Studies, Wednesday includes Spelling Drill, Thursday includes Current Affairs and Friday includes Chapel. The Primary school day closes at 2:00 p.m., with clubs on designated afternoons. RFA operates a 40-week academic year running from September to July, organised into three terms of approximately thirteen weeks. Homework reinforces learning, develops independent study habits and helps teachers and parents understand progress. Learners are expected to complete assigned work carefully and on time; teachers provide guidance and feedback, while parents support a suitable routine and environment for study. Late or incomplete work is handled through the school's academic and conduct procedures.",
